  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/sep100-700.html",
  "prefLabel": "Sep 401.04 Denial of Renewal",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Sep 401.04 Denial of Renewal.\n\n(a) Renewal applications shall be denied if, the licensing bureau finds:\n\n(1) Noncompliance with the continuing education requirements of Sep 403.01;\n\n(2) Any unethical act for which discipline shall be imposed under RSA 310-A:205;\n\n(3) Reasons for which an initial application could be denied; or\n\n(4) Failure to furnish complete or accurate information on an initial or renewal license application.\n\n(b) Any applicant who has been refused a license may request a petition for rehearing pursuant to Plc 311.16.\n\nSource. #12654, eff 10-31-18; ss by #14361, eff 10-26-25, EXPIRES: 10-26-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/sep100-700.html"
